# On Your Left — environment variable template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.gitignore` ignores
# `.env` and `.env.*` and un-ignores this file, so the template is committed and
# the values never are. Never put a real secret here: this repository is public,
# secret scanning with push protection is on, and a pushed commit is permanent
# regardless of what a later commit deletes.
#
# `bash scripts/check-env-example.sh` (rule ENV001) fails if any source file
# under `apps/` or `packages/` reads a variable that is not listed here, so this
# file cannot silently fall behind the code.
#
# Format: one `NAME=placeholder` per line. A variable with no meaningful
# placeholder still gets an entry with an empty value, because the entry is what
# documents that the variable exists.
#
# --- The client -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The client needs no server, no account and no API key: a rider with no
# instance loses nothing (ADR 0036 D-3). The one entry below is the address of a
# *static file* on storage this project controls, and there is no key, no
# account and no metering behind it.

# The PMTiles basemap archive the ride map reads (#63).
#
# ADR 0010 decision D-1: the Protomaps basemap as a PMTiles archive on
# Cloudflare R2, behind Cloudflare's CDN. An `https:` URL to the archive itself;
# no `pmtiles://` prefix, which the client adds.
#
# **Empty means the archive #53 published, which is the default since #534.**
# That is https://tiles.openzigs.com/basemap-us-20260914.pmtiles — the
# Protomaps basemap build of 2026-09-14, copied into this project's own bucket:
# the contiguous United States (longitude -125 to -66, latitude 24 to 50), zoom
# 0 to 15, about 19 GB. The default lives in
# `apps/web/src/map/basemap.ts` §`PUBLISHED_BASEMAP_URL` rather than here,
# because this file is a template nobody's build reads and `.gitignore` refuses
# a committed `.env.production`. So `pnpm run build`, and the APK
# `release.yml` builds, render tiles with nothing set.
#
# Set it to override the default — a self-hoster's own copy, or a different
# extract. Set it to `none` for a build with no basemap and no tile request at
# all. Anything set that is not an `https:` URL (`none`, a typo, an `http:`
# address) means "no basemap", NOT the default: a value somebody set names the
# host they meant, and the ride detail view says "no basemap" in words rather
# than drawing an empty grid.
#
# ⚠️ Outside the archive's coverage the map draws the ride's line on a plain
# background and requests no tiles. There are no labels anywhere: the style
# emits no glyphs and no sprite, because both would need a font host.
#
# ⚠️ **Do not point it at somebody else's host.** Protomaps' own downloads page
# says hotlinking "are discouraged" and "URLs may change", and ADR 0010 D-1 is
# explicit: copy the archive, do not hotlink it. The origin of whatever is here
# is the *only* host the map is permitted to reach, which
# `apps/web/src/map/basemap.test.ts` asserts — and it is disclosed by name in
# `docs/privacy-policy.md`, which a different default host would have to be too.
VITE_BASEMAP_PMTILES_URL=

# --- The instance server (apps/instance, ADR 0036, #767) ---------------------
#
# Read by `apps/instance/src/serve.ts` (and the data paths by
# `src/operator/cli.ts`) and nothing else. None of them is a secret. The Dockerfile sets the host, the port and the commit itself; these
# are for running the instance any other way (`pnpm --filter
# @onyourleft/instance start`).

# The address the instance listens on. Empty means 127.0.0.1, which is right
# for a machine where something else (a tunnel, a proxy) forwards to it; the
# Docker image sets 0.0.0.0, because inside a container 127.0.0.1 is reachable
# from nothing outside it.
OYL_INSTANCE_HOST=

# The TCP port. Empty means 8787. 0 asks the operating system for a free one.
OYL_INSTANCE_PORT=

# The full 40-character commit this build was made from. `GET /source` answers
# with this repository's tree at that commit — the source offer AGPL-3.0 §13
# requires of a server people use over a network (ADR 0036 D-6). ⚠️ The
# instance REFUSES TO START with neither this nor OYL_INSTANCE_SOURCE_URL set,
# because the only other answer is `main`, which is not what is running.
OYL_INSTANCE_COMMIT=

# Where the source of THIS build is, for an operator who modified it — and so
# owes the offer for their own changes, not ours. An `https:` URL; it wins over
# the URL OYL_INSTANCE_COMMIT would give. Empty for an unmodified build.
OYL_INSTANCE_SOURCE_URL=

# What this instance is called, as a rider's app shows it once connected
# (`GET /instance`, #777). At most 64 characters, with no control,
# bidirectional or invisible character. Empty: the instance has no name, and
# the app names it by its address instead.
OYL_INSTANCE_NAME=

# --- Registration and moderation (#775, #83) ---------------------------------
#
# See docs/moderation.md before you open an instance to other people.

# How the instance takes new riders: open, approval, invite or closed (any
# case). EMPTY MEANS closed: nobody new registers, and existing athletes still
# sign in. The project's own image sets approval (the owner's rulings #16, Q5
# and Q13): an account waits for the owner or the deputy to approve it.
OYL_INSTANCE_REGISTRATION=

# The two moderators, each named by a DEVICE KEY — the 64 lower-case hex
# characters of their phone's or browser's public key, which the app shows. A
# key rather than an account, so the owner can be named before registering;
# a named key registers active in every mode. Not secrets: a public key is in
# every ride its device signs.
OYL_INSTANCE_OWNER_KEY=
OYL_INSTANCE_DEPUTY_KEY=

# Public-room eligibility (#775): how many whole days old an account must be,
# and how many rides it must have synced. Empty means 7 and 3. Eligibility also
# needs an approved, unsuspended account whose rider confirmed they are 18 or
# over (ruling Q5); no date of birth is ever collected.
OYL_INSTANCE_PUBLIC_ROOM_MIN_ACCOUNT_DAYS=
OYL_INSTANCE_PUBLIC_ROOM_MIN_RIDES=

# The header a proxy YOU run puts the rider's own address in, for the
# per-address rate limits: cf-connecting-ip behind a Cloudflare Tunnel. Read
# only when the connection comes from loopback or from an address listed in
# OYL_INSTANCE_TRUSTED_PROXIES; from anywhere else it is ignored. Empty means
# the connection's own address, which behind a proxy is the proxy's — one
# bucket for everybody.
OYL_INSTANCE_CLIENT_ADDRESS_HEADER=

# The proxies that header is believed from BESIDES loopback, as exact
# addresses separated by commas (#891's review, #903 item 4). Empty means
# loopback only. ONE rule: the header is read only when it is set AND the
# connection comes from loopback or from one of these. Under
# apps/instance/deploy/home/compose.yaml it is cloudflared's fixed address on
# the compose network, 172.30.87.10, which compose sets for you.
# In Docker by hand with cloudflared on the host, list the bridge gateway
# (usually 172.17.0.1) AND publish the port on 127.0.0.1 only
# (docker run -p 127.0.0.1:8787:8787): published on every interface, anybody
# on the internet arrives from that gateway. docs/moderation.md says more.
OYL_INSTANCE_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# --- The history index (#835, ADR 0040) --------------------------------------
#
# A searchable index of each rider's synced write-ups, ride summaries, goals,
# notes and documents, which the app's analysis may ask for. It is worked out
# by an embedding model on THIS machine or its private network, and nowhere
# else. Empty means no index: the instance starts, says so in its log, and a
# rider's write-up is written without their history.

# The embedding model server's address, alone: http://ollama:11434 for the
# `ollama` service of apps/instance/deploy/home/compose.yaml. ⚠️ REFUSED (and
# the index is then off) unless its host is localhost, a loopback or private
# address, or a single-label name such as a Compose service name; and every
# name is resolved on every request, and refused if it resolves anywhere else.
# ⚠️ Ollama's API has NO authentication: never publish its port and never route
# it through the tunnel.
OYL_INSTANCE_EMBEDDING_URL=

# The model. Empty means nomic-embed-text (nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5,
# Apache-2.0, 768 dimensions), pulled with `ollama pull nomic-embed-text`. Any
# other model you name is yours to choose; changing it re-embeds everything.
OYL_INSTANCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# What goes before every passage and every query. Empty means nomic-embed-text's
# own (`search_document: ` and `search_query: `) for that model, and nothing for
# any other. Changing either re-embeds everything.
OYL_INSTANCE_EMBEDDING_DOCUMENT_PREFIX=
OYL_INSTANCE_EMBEDDING_QUERY_PREFIX=

# --- The analysis model (#1096, ADR 0046 D-9) ------------------------------
# The OpenAI-compatible base URL of a model server on THIS machine or its
# private network — Ollama's is `http://ollama:11434/v1` beside the instance in
# Compose. Loopback, a private address or a single-label name only: a public
# name and `.local` are refused, and where a name resolves to is checked on
# every request. Empty means analysis is off.
OYL_INSTANCE_ANALYSIS_MODEL_URL=

# The model you pulled. There is no default, and this project recommends none
# (ADR 0031 D-4). Empty with a URL set means analysis is off, and says so.
OYL_INSTANCE_ANALYSIS_MODEL=

# The operator's secret a hosted model key is encrypted under (#1097): 32
# bytes, base64 — `openssl rand -base64 32` makes one. Keep it OUT of the
# backups: a snapshot holds the key's ciphertext only, and is no use without
# this. Read by the server and by `node src/operator/cli.ts model-key …`; the
# key is held for the operator, the athlete whose device holds
# OYL_INSTANCE_OWNER_KEY (docs/operating-an-instance.md, "A hosted model
# key"). Empty means no hosted key can be set or read; anything that is not
# 32 bytes of base64 is refused.
# Since #1189 the instance's own identity and encryption keys are wrapped under
# it too (ADR 0047 D-5): set, the server makes them on its first start; unset,
# it makes none and /v1/instance/keys answers unavailable. Losing it loses the
# keys, and every device pins again (docs/operating-an-instance.md, "The
# instance's keys").
OYL_INSTANCE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- The running server (#780, #791) ----------------------------------------

# The SQLite database file. Empty means data/instance.sqlite under the working
# directory; the Docker image sets /data/instance.sqlite, on its one volume.
# ⚠️ The instance NEVER migrates it: run `node src/operator/cli.ts migrate`
# first (the deploy's migrate step, #791), or it refuses to start.
OYL_INSTANCE_DATABASE=

# The blob directory, backed up with the database. Empty means data/blobs.
OYL_INSTANCE_BLOBS=

# This instance's public origin, as a rider's device signs it: the tunnel's
# hostname, `https://rides.example.org`. `https:` unless it is this machine.
# Empty serves no accounts: every identity route answers `unavailable` (503),
# so no ticket can be minted and no room joined.
OYL_INSTANCE_ORIGIN=

# How many room-worker processes. Empty means one per core, which is what a
# box needs (spike 0013 §4.1: one event loop is one core).
OYL_INSTANCE_ROOM_WORKERS=

# `on` accepts WebSocket compression (permessage-deflate) on room sockets.
# Empty or `off` is the default (ruling Q16): compression halves the upload
# and doubles the memory (ADR 0037 D-3). On a home connection whose UPLOAD is
# the limit (#807), turning it on can double the rooms it carries.
OYL_INSTANCE_WS_COMPRESSION=

# How often the instance pings every room socket, in milliseconds. Empty means
# 25000: under the 30 s client keepalive (ADR 0037 D-8.1) and well under the
# ~100 s idle timeout reported for Cloudflare's proxy. 0 sends no ping — ONLY
# to measure a tunnel's own idle timeout (docs/self-hosting/home-machine.md),
# never to run with.
OYL_INSTANCE_PING_INTERVAL_MS=

# `on` serves GET /metrics (Prometheus text): riders, rooms, tick lateness,
# worker memory, refusals. Off by default. No label names a rider, a room or
# a coordinate (#791). With it on, OYL_INSTANCE_METRICS_TOKEN is REQUIRED.
OYL_INSTANCE_METRICS=

# The bearer token /metrics answers (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`); any
# other request gets 404, as if metrics were off. At least 32 characters —
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. ⚠️ A secret: the box's .env only, never a commit.
OYL_INSTANCE_METRICS_TOKEN=

# --- The home deployment (#807, #52) -----------------------------------------
#
# Read by `apps/instance/deploy/home/compose.yaml` and `deploy.sh`, from the
# `.env` beside them (template: `instance.env.example` there). The guide is
# docs/self-hosting/home-machine.md.

# The image to run. deploy.sh sets it to the tag it built; a hand-run
# `docker compose` uses `onyourleft-instance:local`, which deploy.sh tags.
OYL_INSTANCE_IMAGE=

# The token Cloudflare's dashboard gives the tunnel. ⚠️ A SECRET: it goes in
# the box's `.env` and nowhere else — never a commit, never a log, never here.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# Where the scheduled backup writes its snapshots on the box, and where it
# copies each one OFF the box (a USB drive, a share). Both required.
OYL_BACKUP_DIR=
OYL_OFFBOX_DIR=

# How many snapshots to keep in each place (default 14), and how often to take
# one, in seconds (default 21600: every six hours).
OYL_BACKUP_KEEP=
OYL_BACKUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=

# How long deploy.sh waits for the new build to say /ready before it rolls
# back by itself, in seconds. Default 120.
OYL_DEPLOY_READY_SECONDS=

# --- An S3-compatible bucket, for the blob store's conformance suite (#770) --
#
# ⚠️ **Read by a TEST, not by the instance yet**:
# `apps/instance/src/blob/s3-blob-store.test.ts` runs the blob store
# conformance suite against this bucket when all five are set, and SKIPS LOUDLY
# naming them when any is not. Not a CI gate — CI sets none of them. The
# instance itself keeps blobs on local disk (ADR 0002 A); choosing a bucket at
# run time is the first consumer's to wire (#37).
#
# ⚠️ The suite writes and then deletes a handful of small objects keyed by their
# SHA-256. Point it at a bucket you use for nothing else. The secret is a
# secret: set it in your shell, never in a committed file.
OYL_INSTANCE_S3_ENDPOINT=
OYL_INSTANCE_S3_BUCKET=
OYL_INSTANCE_S3_REGION=
OYL_INSTANCE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
OYL_INSTANCE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- The browser gate, not the product --------------------------------------
#
# A hosted PMTiles archive for the browser gate to measure against (#63).
#
# ⚠️ **Not read by anything that ships.** It is read by
# `apps/web/browser/map.browser.spec.ts`, which is Playwright rather than Vite —
# hence no `VITE_` prefix, which would only put it in a bundle. Unset, it skips
# the hosted block of `pnpm run test:browser`, and CI leaves it unset: a gate
# that needs somebody else's CDN is a gate that fails on an aeroplane. Set to an
# `https:` archive URL, that block renders the real basemap in the pinned
# Chromium and takes #63's eighth measurement, time to first painted tile.
#
# ⚠️ Set but malformed is an **error**, not a skip. "Nothing configured" and
# "configured wrongly" are different states and only the first is a reason to
# measure nothing — `apps/web/browser/hosted-archive.ts` says why.
#
# ⚠️ Deliberately a different name from VITE_BASEMAP_PMTILES_URL above. Reusing
# that one would silently put a network dependency into the browser gate for
# everybody who has a basemap configured for their own development build.
OYL_HOSTED_BASEMAP_URL=

# --- The device probe, not the product ---------------------------------------
#
# The local TCP port `adb forward` is holding open onto the shell's WebView
# DevTools socket (#410).
#
# ⚠️ **Not read by anything that ships, and not read by any gate either.** It is
# read by `apps/mobile/tools/webview-probe.mjs`, which needs `adb`, a phone with
# developer options on and a **debug** build — so it can never run in CI and is
# not part of `check:repo`. `docs/validation/0002-android-shell-and-game.md`
# Part P is the procedure it serves.
#
# Unset, the probe uses 9222, which is what `adb forward tcp:9222 …` gives you
# and what every DevTools example on the internet assumes. Set it when 9222 is
# already taken on your machine, and forward to the same number.
OYL_DEVTOOLS_PORT=9222

# --- The realistic world's asset pipeline, not the product ---------------------
#
# Where Blender is, for `pnpm --filter @onyourleft/web run realistic:process`
# (#430, ADR 0026 D-5). Empty means the macOS app's own path,
# /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender.
#
# ⚠️ **Not read by anything that ships, and not read by any gate.** Blender is a
# tool and never a dependency: CI does not run it, and the pipeline refuses any
# version but the one it is pinned to (`apps/web/tools/realistic/sources.ts`
# §`PINNED_BLENDER`), because a different Blender may decimate differently and
# the committed bytes would describe a run nobody can repeat.
BLENDER=

# Where KTX-Software's `ktx` is, for the same `realistic:process` (#618, ADR 0026
# D-8's 2026-09-27 amendment). Empty means `ktx` on the PATH, which is where
# the release's own installer puts it.
#
# ⚠️ **A tool, like Blender, and read by nothing that ships and no gate.** The
# pipeline refuses any version but the pinned one (`apps/web/tools/realistic/
# sources.ts` §`PINNED_KTX`, which also says how it was installed), because a
# different encoder makes different blocks.
KTX=

# --- The display face's subsetting step, not the product ----------------------
#
# The Python that runs fontTools, for `pnpm --filter @onyourleft/web run
# fonts:subset` (#991, ADR 0043). Empty means `python3` on the PATH.
#
# ⚠️ **A tool, like Blender: read by nothing that ships and by no gate.** The
# step refuses any fontTools but 4.66.1 and any Brotli but 1.2.0
# (`apps/web/tools/fonts/font-recipe.ts` §`PINNED_FONTTOOLS`), because a
# different version may write different WOFF2 bytes. `subset-fonts.ts`' header
# says how to make a virtual environment with exactly those.
FONTTOOLS_PYTHON=

# --- The sentence record, not the product -------------------------------------
#
# Set to 1 to RE-RECORD `apps/web/src/a11y/route-sentences.snapshot.json`: every
# sentence every route renders, over both walk fixtures (#666, "nothing is
# deleted"). Unset — always, in CI — the test only reads the record and fails
# for any sentence a route no longer renders.
#
# ⚠️ **Re-recording is a decision, not a repair.** The record was taken on
# `main` before #666 changed any screen; re-taking it on a branch that lost a
# sentence records the loss as correct. Reword a sentence by editing the record
# in the same commit instead, where a reviewer reads both halves.
OYL_RECORD_ROUTE_SENTENCES=
